+# Service-calendar authoring and release boundary
+
+## Source ownership
+
+- Edit `service-calendar.tera` and its three adjacent `service-calendar-*.js` sources.
+- `tools/spotless-cli/assemble-service-calendar.tether` assembles those sources only.
+- The result is `tools/spotless-cli/template-payloads/service-calendar.generated.tera`.
+  It contains its controller inline; no separately deployed booking JavaScript bundle is needed.
+- **Do not hand-edit `tools/spotless-cli/spotless_cli.tether`.** It remains generated
+  from OpenAPI using the existing CLI generator and templates. New API operations
+  must enter that CLI through normal contract generation, not registry patches.
+- Do not publish the unassembled authoring template: its assembly markers are not
+  executable controller implementations.
+
+Local assembly (does not contact any API):
+
+```sh
+tetherscript run tools/spotless-cli/assemble-service-calendar.tether
+```
+
+## Customer workflow
+
+The component requires a real quote, same-origin endpoint, and quote-bound booking
+credential. It never manufactures preview slots. Availability supplies the actual
+quote price, currency, service name, capacity-backed slots, and operations timezone.
+
+- Availability: Rust `GET /api/exterior-booking/{quote_id}/availability` proxies to
+  Fastify `POST /orpc/exterior-quotes/booking-availability`.
+- Hold: Rust `POST /api/exterior-booking/{quote_id}/reserve` proxies to
+  Fastify `POST /orpc/exterior-quotes/reserve-booking`.
+- Decline: Rust `POST /api/exterior-booking/{quote_id}/release` proxies to
+  Fastify `POST /orpc/exterior-quotes/release-booking`. The exact displayed window
+  must match. Stripe must confirm cancellation before capacity is released.
+- Charge: Rust `POST /api/exterior-booking/authorize-charge` proxies to Fastify
+  `POST /orpc/exterior-quotes/authorize-booking-charge`. Expired or changed holds
+  are rejected; confirmed collection and confirmed scheduling are separate results.
+
+Credentials travel in the customer header and server-side request body, never the URL.
+Do not log them or save them in test artifacts.
+
+## Production gate
+
+Local assembly is **static/local evidence only**. Before customer rollout:
+
+1. Run authorized API/Rust builds and regenerate API/CLI artifacts normally.
+2. Deploy the compatible backend routes before publishing this component.
+3. Resolve the current `service_calendar` registry and placements; never blindly
+   reuse restored numeric component/version IDs from old publication artifacts.
+4. With explicit permission and real operations data, exercise both API surfaces,
+   hold contention/expiry, cancellation retries, payment consent, scheduling,
+   receipt delivery, and the operations-visible booking record.
+
+No production booking, charge, cancellation, deployment, or publication was performed
+by the local assembly script. Until the production gate is satisfied, this is not
+evidence that the customer booking flow is ready to ship.
